.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-history - Show a payment's chronological history


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments history  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the timeline of everything that happened to a payment since it was
created: the created and signed milestones and every on-chain transaction
(authorize/capture/void/release/refund/dispute/close_dispute), oldest first.
Only the most significant fields are shown per entry (time, event, status,
amount, tx hash, block).

.PP
The argument is a UUID or a rail0_id (0x…, 64 hex). Requires login — the
timeline is readable only by the payment's payer or payee.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for history


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments history 0xabc123…
  rail0 payments history 019e748b-…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
